270
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,000
we try to celebrate accomplishments

271
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
and minimize failures.

272
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
and that healthy peer pressure.

273
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,000
it's a very positive thing,

274
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,000
not only for our older

275
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,000
scouts but for our younger ones as well.

276
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,000
Number seven: we try

277
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,000
and build an atmosphere

278
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,000
of respect, real concern

279
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
and care for the welfare of our younger

280
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
scouts. We make it the first

281
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
priority of everyone

282
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
in the troop. We monitor for

283
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
any kind of cruelty or bullying or hazing

284
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
and we manage it right as soon

285
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
as we know about it.

286
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
This is another one of those things that

287
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,000
you can't get too worked up

288
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,000
about when it occurs,

289
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
because it's something that you should

290
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,000
expect and you should be prepared to handle.

291
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,000
Again, not a boys

292
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,000
will be boys atmosphere

293
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,000
of permissiveness, but

294
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,000
authoritative leadership from the adults

295
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
when these types of things happen

296
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
and we step in and we make what

297
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
corrections we need and

298
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:39,000
we keep that positive emphasis

299
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
in all of our actions.

300
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Number eight: we don't nitpick

301
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,000
the decisions made by our older scouts

302
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:47,000
that offer much in the way of unsolicited

303
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,000
advice. Do you remember how you learned

304
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,000
