00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:45,000
Hey, here's some email questions that have come in.

426
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:47,000
John Hibner is in Indiana

427
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,000
And he says: do you have any suggestions

428
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
On how to get a dysfunctional troop to turn the corner

429
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:55,000
And operate properly using the patrol method?

430
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:58,000
Our troop historically has had about 20 active scouts.

431
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:01,000
We've managed to get a handful of older scouts

432
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:03,000
To the youth leader training,

433
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:06,000
But it seems to wear off in a matter of months.

434
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:08,000
I have an inter-battle, like most scout leaders,

435
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:11,000
With keeping from interfering with troop operations,

436
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:14,000
But it's frustrating for me because it seems

437
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:17,000
Boys never get to the point where they operate

438
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:20,000
As scouting was intended 90% of the time

439
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,000
And, truth be told, sometimes our troop

440
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:25,000
Is nothing better than a loosely organized boys club

441
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:27,000
Where all they want to do is play a game

442
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:29,000
During the entire meeting.

443
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:31,000
Well, John, a lot of this begins, of course,

444
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:34,000
With the adults who are involved with the troop,

445
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:36,000
And you all need to sit down

446
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:38,000
And kind of hit the reset button

447
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:40,000
And say: what are we really trying to do here

448
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,000
And do a little bit of studying

449
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:44,000
And talking amongst yourselves.

450
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:46,000
Let the boys play games in their meetings. for now-

451
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:48,000
And you'll get to that later-

452
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:50,000
The first thing you've got to do

453
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:52,000
Is you've got to get all the adults

454
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:54,000
Who are involved with the troop on the same page

455
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,000
And make a commitment to this.

456
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,000
Then you need to realize that the patrol method

457
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:01,000
And youth leadership is not throwing a switch.

458
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:03,000
It's not either, or

459
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:05,000
It's not. well, the boys just play games

460
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,000
For every meeting because you know

461
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:10,000
It's a boy-led troop and this is what they wanted to do.

462
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Nope, they need some structure

463
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,000
And they need some information.

464
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,000
Now you would think that you would be able

465
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:18,000
To send them to youth leader training

466
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:20,000
And they would get that structure and information

467
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
And they would bring it back to the troop.

468
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,000
But that is not a very common occurrence,

469
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,000
To tell you the truth.

470
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
Youth leader training is a good start,

471
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,000
But unless the adults in the troop

472
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,000
Are ready to work with the structure

473
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:34,000
And information that was imparted

474
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:36,000
At youth leader training,

475
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:38,000
Things are going to wear off.

476
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:40,000
The corner you're going to turn

477
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,000
Is going to begin with the adults.

478
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:44,000
You're going to sit down

479
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:46,000
And you're going to sort things out

480
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:48,000
And shape an attitude in the scouts

481
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:50,000
Where they understand the importance

482
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:52,000
Of these things and they begin

483
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:54,000
Putting them into practice.

484
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:56,000
What this looks like from where you sit

485
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:58,000
And what it looks like

486
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:00,000
From where the scouts are

487
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:02,000
Is a trick of perspective.

488
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:04,000
We've said over and over again

489
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:06,000
That when the patrol method is in practice

490
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:08,000
It can look very messy

491
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:10,000
And disorganized and chaotic.

492
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:12,000
But you need to develop

493
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:14,000
And cultivate the perspective

494
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:16,000
For seeing that it's working.

495
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:18,000
Boys have a lot of instinctual ability

496
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:20,000
To do this

497
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:22,000
But they're kind of

498
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:24,000
Stumbling through it

499
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:26,000
And working it out as they go along

500
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,000
And it looks like a mess

501
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:30,000
And you need to learn to look for

502
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:32,000
Those encouraging signs

503
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,000
That they're beginning to get it

504
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:36,000
And then cultivating that

505
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:38,000
As they go along.

506
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:40,000
But it's a big job

507
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:42,000
But it's very, very possible

508
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:44,000
And it certainly works.

509
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:46,000
John, I hope that helped.

